      "description": "Same physical input on both sides; the follow-up case multiplies OpenMC's `particles` count by factor > 1. By the Monte-Carlo 1/√N sampling law the reported k_eff_std must shrink to ~ 1/√factor of the source value. The variance-ratio assertion permits a (1 + ToleranceRel) relative slack above the expected ratio to absorb finite-sample noise.",
